:"This gene encodes a highly conserved enzyme that belongs to the aminoacyl-tRNA synthetase class IIc subfamily. This enzyme comprises the regulatory beta subunits that form a tetramer with two catalytic alpha subunits. In the presence of ATP, this tetramer is responsible for attaching L-phenylalanine to the terminal adenosine of the appropriate tRNA. A pseudogene located on chromosome 10 has been identified. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Jan 2015].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[],"uniprot_source":null,"retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}